IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp1-nouns`
IMPORT `cp1-div-a-pensionable-employment`

-- Tests of cp1-div-a-pensionable-employment.l4: sections 5, 6 and 7(4).
-- Every expected value was decided from the text of the section (the line numbers are in the module) before
-- the file was run. Generated from a hand-written case list; the expectations are written beside each assertion.
-- A case record names only what matters; the other facts are those of an ordinary job in Canada paid 40,000
-- dollars in cash for 200 working days.

§ `Tests -- sections 5, 6 and 7(4)`

-- case 1: an ordinary job in Canada
`employment case 1: an ordinary job in Canada` MEANS `cp1 Facts about an employment` WITH
    `the employment is in Canada` IS TRUE
    `the employment is under Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS FALSE
    `a regulation made under section 7 includes the employment in pensionable employment` IS FALSE
    `a regulation made under section 7 excepts the employment from pensionable employment` IS FALSE
    `the employment is in agriculture or an agricultural enterprise, horticulture, fishing, hunting, trapping, forestry, logging or lumbering` IS FALSE
    `cash remuneration the employer pays the employee in the year` IS 40_000
    `the employer employs the employee on terms providing for payment of cash remuneration` IS TRUE
    `working days in the year for which the employer so employs the employee` IS 200
    `the employment is of a casual nature` IS FALSE
    `the employment is for the purpose of the employer's trade or business` IS TRUE
    `the employee is a teacher on exchange from a country other than Canada` IS FALSE
    `the employee is employed by the employee's spouse or common-law partner` IS FALSE
    `the remuneration paid may be deducted under the Income Tax Act in computing the income of the spouse or common-law partner` IS FALSE
    `the employee is a member of a religious order who has taken a vow of perpetual poverty` IS FALSE
    `the remuneration is paid either directly or by the member to the order` IS FALSE
    `no cash remuneration is paid` IS FALSE
    `the employee is the child of the employer` IS FALSE
    `the employee is maintained by the employer` IS FALSE
    `the employment is as a member of the Canadian Forces or the Royal Canadian Mounted Police` IS FALSE
    `another Act of Parliament provides otherwise for that employment` IS FALSE
    `the employer employs persons in Canada` IS TRUE
    `a reciprocal agreement between the Government of Canada and the government of another country exempts the employer from liability to make the contributions imposed on an employer by this Act` IS FALSE
    `the employment is by Her Majesty in right of a province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province` IS FALSE
    `the employment is by the government of a country other than Canada or by an international organization` IS FALSE
    `the employee is an Indian as defined in the Indian Act` IS FALSE
    `the earnings from the employment are not included in computing income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 6(2) — the employment is excepted employment` `employment case 1: an ordinary job in Canada` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(a) — the employment is employment in Canada that is not excepted employment` `employment case 1: an ordinary job in Canada` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) — the employment is employment in Canada under Her Majesty in right of Canada that is not excepted employment` `employment case 1: an ordinary job in Canada` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(c) — the employment is included in pensionable employment by a regulation made under section 7` `employment case 1: an ordinary job in Canada` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1) — the employment is pensionable employment` `employment case 1: an ordinary job in Canada` EQUALS TRUE

